{
  "name": "Back-dated MTM valuations for counterparty audit requests",
  "today": "Counterparties' auditors need third-party mark-to-market (MTM) values of their deals with Enron as of a past date, usually year end. Confirmations (Larry Joe Hunter, Ellen Wallumrod) must provide them but has no system that values deals. So for each request it emails all six Risk desk heads (Gossett, Keiser, Love, Giron, Baumbach, McLaughlin). Each desk head forwards it to an analyst on the desk (for the West desk, Giron sends it on to Pat Ryder). The analyst runs a back-dated mini-book for the counterparty, exports it to Excel and emails back the totals for the region. Confirmations then has to black out the Delta/Vol data in the mini-books before anything goes out, and combines the regional replies.",
  "change": "Finish the planned EnTelligence view (or a similar report) with back-dated curves, so Confirmations can value a counterparty's deals for a past date without asking six Risk desks.",
  "explanation": "Confirmations already plans this. Build the on-line EnTelligence view (or an equivalent report) that keeps back-dated price curves and shows only the columns a counterparty may see, with no Delta/Vol. When an auditor's request arrives, Hunter or Wallumrod enter the counterparty and the date, check the result and send it. Desk heads no longer read and forward requests, no Risk analyst in any region runs a mini-book, and nothing has to be blacked out.",
  "occurrences": [
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/240.eml",
      "quote": "Please forward to Ellen Wallumrod the MTM valuation(mini-book) for all \nCoEnergy Trading Company deals as of Dec 31, 2000.  If you can export into \nexcel and forward by e-mail, that would be appreciated."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/214.eml",
      "quote": "Can you provide MTM values as of Dec 29, 2000, for the short name of CROSS \nTIMBERS."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/137.eml",
      "quote": "Two more counterparties need MTM values for Dec. 29, 2000."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/136.eml",
      "quote": "The following are the totals for Tudor BVI and Ospraie.  The total MTM value \nfor the West Desk are as follows."
    }
  ],
  "evidence": [
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/241.eml",
      "quote": "Until we can get EnTelligence built to our specifications, \nwe'll need to continue to go to the different desks to provide Mark-to-Market \nvaluations for a Counterparty's portfolio.",
      "note": "Each request goes to every Risk desk because Confirmations cannot value the deals itself, and the fix is already planned."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/241.eml",
      "quote": "We do not have access to \nany system that values these deals, but are looking to get the on-line \n\"EnTelligence\" built so that it carries back-dated curves that will allow us \nto complete these requests without taking up a Risk person's time and without \nhaving to black out information (Delta/Vol) that is included in a mini-book.",
      "note": "The change removes the Risk analysts' time and Confirmations' blacking out of Delta/Vol data."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/137.eml",
      "quote": "Please provide the total MTM value for that date within your region.",
      "note": "Every region is asked to work out its own total, so one request causes work on each of the six desks."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/214.eml",
      "quote": "To: Jeffrey C Gossett/HOU/ECT@ECT, Kam Keiser/HOU/ECT@ECT, Phillip M \nLove/HOU/ECT@ECT, Darron C Giron/HOU/ECT@ECT, David Baumbach/HOU/ECT@ECT, \nErrol McLaughlin/Corp/Enron@ENRON",
      "note": "One request goes to all six desk heads, who each pass it to an analyst (Giron forwards this one to Patrick Ryder)."
    }
  ],
  "stalls": [],
  "ongoing": true,
  "stated_rate": {
    "count": 3,
    "per": "week",
    "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/241.eml",
    "quote": "we recieve several \nper week"
  },
  "minutes": 75
}

