}

{
  "name": "Weekly manual compaction of WeaponX Access databases",
  "change": "IT runs an unattended overnight compact of every WeaponX file, with a rolling backup and a daily size check, so book admins stop compacting by hand.",
  "reason": "The same work and change, citing the same two messages (giron-d/sent/585.eml and 596.eml), is already saved as item 2 in decisions.md, 'Weekly manual compaction of WeaponX Access databases'.",
  "research": null
}

{
  "name": "Daily Credit Report wrong-entity rebooks and hand-forwarding to book admins",
  "change": "Add standing counterparty-entity rules to TAGG at deal entry and split the Credit Report by desk so it goes straight to each book admin",
  "reason": "The 40-minute daily saving rests on claims the mail does not support: only Giron is shown forwarding the report (not six desks), repeat mappings come up about once per report company-wide (not four a day for one desk), and the 'standing rules' are not fixed (Louis Dreyfus Natural Gas Holdings is sent to Louis Dreyfus Natural Gas Corp on 3/12 but to Louis Dreyfus Corporation on 3/15; ENA/ECC rebooks go both ways), while auto-booking to ECC already exists for some Canadian counterparties.",
  "research": "Find whether other desk heads (Gossett, Keiser, Love, etc.) also forward the report to admins, and how many lines per report belong to the West book; if not, a resubmission should be limited to adding the West book admin to Credit's distribution list, valued at a few minutes a day."
}

